{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"At one core's rates the NovaSeq 6000 costs 2.3-3.1x the X 25B per Gb on S4 flow cells but ~4-10x on the smaller S2/SP flow cells, so a tail made up of small users would explain Illumina's 3.4x revenue-per-Gb gap without any X repricing.","detail":"Salk (eff. 1 Jul 2025, external nonprofit) prices per Gb are: S4-300 $13.2-16.5, S2-300 $24,938 for 3.3-4.1B pairs × 300 (~0.99-1.23 Tb) = $20.3-25.2, and SP-300 $10,175 for 0.65-0.8B × 300 (195-240 Gb) = $42-52. The 25B-300 is $5.32-5.67. That is a 6000/X ratio of ~2.3-3.1x (S4), ~3.6-4.7x (S2) and ~7.5-9.8x (SP). The GSA S4-300 vs 25B-300 ratio is ~2.4x ($7.23 vs ~$3.02/Gb), so Illumina's reported 3.4x suggests the remaining 6000 volume skews to smaller flow cells and lower-volume, higher-price users. Those users are the least volume-elastic, which fits the thesis that they convert slowly and that each conversion is a big price step.","url":"https://www.salk.edu/science/core-facilities/integrative-genomics-and-bioinformatics-core/scheduling-and-rates/","date":"2025-07-01","source_name":"Salk IGC rate page; GSA prices (known)","source_type":"price_list","quote":"Rates effective as of 07/01/25 and are subject to change.","strength":"weak","why_new":"Prior core ratios compared only S4 to 25B; this adds the flow-cell-mix explanation for the 3.4x vendor gap.","based_on":["F289","D025","D027"]},
